map between Fr´echet spaces, so �g is a topological isomorphism by Banach’s theorem.

b) If g is surjective, Banach’s theorem implies that g is open, thus g is an epimorphism.
If g(E) is finite codimensional, let S be a supplementary subspace of g(E) in F, dim S <
+∞. Then the map

