+# Batch 66 authoring notes
+
+## Scope and planning evidence
+
+Owned pair: `qftx-gaga-compact-coherent-finiteness` and its examples companion.
+The canonical plan contains one A-page theorem and two B-page examples:
+
+- `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-compact-projective-coherent-finiteness`;
+- `ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-point`;
+- `ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-finite-not-vanishing`.
+
+The current batch manifest still has empty `items` arrays. This is a planning
+placeholder, not a conflict: the current `research/plan-spec.json` and owner
+direction require all three carriers and substantive B-page examples. I will
+populate the authorized batch manifest after writing the carriers.
+
+There is no separate canonical pair-design section governing this pair. The
+owner's `adhm-gaga-analytic-scaffold.md` section 967.18 is a source scaffold,
+not a competing plan: its statement, dependencies, examples and proof
+obligations match the current canonical plan. The current plan therefore
+controls. No conflicting claim or convention was found.
+
+The current batch-level graph records batch 66 at level 2 with page prerequisites
+from batches 63 and 65. The plan's item-level proposals are theorem level 3 and
+examples level 4, reflecting the planned item suppliers' levels 1 and 2. These
+are different graph levels, not a conflict. I will recompute item levels after
+any local A-page intermediates are added.
+
+## In-run prerequisites and readiness
+
+I loaded the live snapshot with `loadStep1Record` and checked relevant IDs with
+`step1Decision` from `tools/physics-support/step1-decisions.mjs`. The live batch
+63 A/B manifest contains seven full item records, including the exact planned
+`thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-oka-coherence` carrier. Its existing non-owner `ready`
+record is hash-stale (`Item or dependency changed; record current readiness`).
+I read its full current statement and proof; the interface matches the plan, so
+the proof is used conditionally pending a current readiness record. I do not
+alter batch 63 or overwrite its record.
+
+The live batch 65 manifest also has full items, but the exact planned supplier
+ID `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-local-coherent-polydisc-acyclicity` is absent. It
+instead manifests `thm-qftx-gaga-local-coherent-acyclicity`, whose full current
+statement and proof I inspected. Its statement includes the planned local
+vanishing interface and additional scalar Dolbeault and resolution-length
+claims. The two IDs are not silently substituted: the planned-ID readiness
+check returns `Readiness record missing`, and the manifested alternate's check
+also returns `Readiness record missing`. The exact planned interface in
+`research/plan-spec.json` is: for coherent analytic `G` near `x` in `C^N`, a
+coordinate polydisc `W` exists such that every nonempty coordinate polydisc
+`D⊂W` has ordinary `H^q(D,G|D)=0` for every `q>0`; it is local and makes no
+global Cartan A/B claim. The consuming proof uses precisely that interface,
+conditionally, on cover members only.
+
+The batch 65 manifest also contains
+`lem-qftx-gaga-euclidean-sheaf-cohomological-dimension`; its full ordinary
+cohomology proof was inspected and is used for dimension shifting. Its Step 1
+record is missing, as is the current record for its in-run metric Čech
+comparison input. The finite-polyhedron imported result's open-subspace clause
+concerns compact-support cohomology and is not used as ordinary cohomology.
+
+The intersection argument separately proves pseudoconvex geometry for finite
+intersections of coordinate polydiscs, scalar Dolbeault acyclicity, and coherent
+dimension shifting conditional on the exact Oka interface. Neither the planned
+local-polydisc theorem nor its alternate is applied to arbitrary intersections.
+These current stale/missing readiness and item-identity issues keep the target
+and the consuming helpers escalated until the owner supplies current exact
+carriers/records.
+
+## Sources read
+
+1. Jean-Pierre Demailly, *Complex Analytic and Differential Geometry*,
+   <https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf>,
+   printed pp. 406–407 (IX.1.8–1.9) and 421–424 (IX.4.3–4.8). I read the full
+   displayed Fréchet/Schwartz proofs and the local-resolution, section-topology,
+   restriction-compactness and Cartan–Serre arguments. The browser PDF open
+   timed out once; an immediate full-text shell retrieval succeeded (3.39 MB,
+   SHA-256 `d7c7654a7417e8322e5dcf8fe8ec818b4c1a18cf280b41f2df5a871b776d89a1`).
+   `source-fetch-check --stamp` remains to be run on the authored citations.
+2. Henri Cartan, “Un théorème de finitude,” *Séminaire Henri Cartan* 6
+   (1953–1954), exposé 17, pp. 1–11,
+   <https://www.numdam.org/item/SHC_1953-1954__6__A17_0.pdf>. I read the
+   complete 12-page scan, including the finite Stein-cover proof, the quotient
+   Fréchet topology, compact restriction, Leray comparison and Schwartz
+   perturbation step. This is a second, original treatment; the site describes
+   the talk and its 11 printed pages.
+3. Yuan Liu, “Cartan’s method and its applications in sheaf cohomology,”
+   <https://arxiv.org/pdf/2204.13185>, §2.1, Theorems 2.2–2.5 (PDF pp. 6–10).
+   Full 12-page PDF retrieved (146.1 KB, SHA-256
+   `22a5a29e61b1b13414b416866229a27cf7cdc64b56ba8451f19da032caa2fe76`). I
+   read the Godement-resolution induction on closed cubes and the local-to-global
+   topological-dimension argument for paracompact manifolds. The in-run helper
+   `lem-qftx-gaga-euclidean-sheaf-cohomological-dimension` carries a full proof
+   of the required ordinary dimension bound from this route.
+
+4. Henri Cartan's Numdam PDF was re-fetched after context compaction from the
+   source URL above; the complete 12-page scan was converted to text and I
+   re-read the cohomology setup, Fréchet quotient topology, compact restriction,
+   Leray comparison, and final Schwartz argument (printed pp. 1–11). The
+   retrieved PDF size is 1,115,990 bytes. This was a successful re-read, not a
+   recovery after a failed retrieval.
+
+No retrieval failure remains unresolved. The original two-page Cartan–Serre
+translation was also opened during source discovery, but the primary Numdam
+seminar text above is the source selected for the authored record. No source
+fetch stamp has yet been written, and no source is marked dropped.
+
+## Actual supplier checks
+
+I read the current imported statements and complete proofs for the direct
+published suppliers used by the planned theorem: `def-axiom-of-choice`,
+`thm-artin-rees-lemma`, `thm-krull-intersection-theorem`,
+`thm-cauchy-estimates-on-a-polydisc`,
+`thm-locally-uniform-limit-of-holomorphic-functions-in-several-variables`,
+`cor-ascoli-arzela-for-compact-metric-domains`,
+`thm-leray-acyclic-cover-theorem`,
+`thm-cech-to-sheaf-cohomology-comparison`, and
+`cor-dolbeault-vanishing-pseudoconvex-domain`. The AC boundary is explicit in
+the choice, Ascoli, Leray/Čech and Dolbeault suppliers, and the target retains
+the full AC assumption.
+
+For the intersection argument I also inspected the exact definition and proofs
+for Hartogs pseudoconvexity, smooth psh-exhaustion regularization, the
+bounded-domain exhaustion-to-Hartogs lemma, scalar Dolbeault vanishing, the
+Euclidean ordinary cohomological-dimension lemma and its refinement supplier,
+the long exact sequence of sheaf cohomology, stalkwise exactness, Godement's
+flasque resolution and flasque acyclicity, and compact-subset section
+extension. The finite-polyhedron result's open-subspace clause remains
+excluded because it concerns compact-support cohomology.
+
+## Authoring checkpoint
+
+The following local A-page carriers are authored with conventions and
+dependencies declared in each item's frontmatter and `Facts & Assumptions`:
+
+- `def-qftx-gaga-frechet-space`: Hausdorff complete metrizable locally convex
+  complex spaces; Demailly IX.1 and Cartan exposé 17.
+- `lem-qftx-gaga-baire-category-complete-metric-spaces` and
+  `lem-qftx-gaga-frechet-open-mapping`: full-AC Baire and Fréchet open mapping,
+  with successive approximation and an explicit neighborhood-series bound.
+- `lem-qftx-gaga-schwartz-compact-perturbation` and
+  `lem-qftx-gaga-frechet-complex-compact-finiteness`: the compact perturbation
+  and compact morphism of Fréchet complexes finite-Hausdorff-cohomology proof.
+- `lem-qftx-gaga-scalar-pseudoconvex-acyclicity` and
+  `lem-qftx-gaga-pseudoconvex-intersection-acyclicity`: scalar Dolbeault
+  resolution; then psh exhaustion, bounded Hartogs pseudoconvexity, scalar
+  Dolbeault vanishing, and conditional length-`2r` Oka dimension shifting using
+  the existing ordinary Euclidean cohomological-dimension lemma.
+- `def-qftx-gaga-coherent-section-topology`,
+  `lem-qftx-gaga-coherent-section-topology-well-defined`, and
+  `lem-qftx-gaga-coherent-section-restriction-compact`: quotient Fréchet
+  topology, Artin–Rees/Krull presentation control, and multivariable compact
+  restriction via Cauchy estimates, Ascoli, and diagonal exhaustion.
+- `lem-qftx-gaga-cstar-laurent-decomposition`: contour coefficient extraction
+  and entire positive/negative Laurent parts on `C*`.
+- `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-compact-projective-coherent-finiteness`: conditional
+  nested polydisc Leray covers, compact cochain restriction, the Fréchet-complex
+  theorem, and topology independence.
+- B examples `ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-point` and
+  `ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-finite-not-vanishing`: finite-support skyscraper
+  decomposition; and the direct two-chart Laurent computation of
+  `H^1(P^1,O(-2))`.
+
+The source locators are the Demailly PDF, Cartan Numdam PDF, Liu arXiv PDF,
+source-item paths identified in each dependency list, and the current batch
+63/65 item files described above. No GAGA comparison, global Cartan A/B,
+experimental claim, or later pair67 input is invoked. The batch 66 A/B page
+frontmatter, complete item manifests, proof contracts, coverage, cross-batch
+dependency array, source-fetch stamps, scoped validation and per-item Step 1
+records remain to be completed.
+
+## Current proof decision and next work
+
+The ordinary cohomological-dimension proof and the non-polydisc intersection
+argument are now carried by explicit local items. The outstanding blockers are
+the hash-stale batch 63 readiness record, the exact batch 65 supplier-ID
+mismatch and missing readiness records for its alternate/local dimension items,
+plus contract/coverage generation and required scoped checks. Consuming proofs
+retain the complete planned supplier statements as conditional assumptions;
+the target and dependent helpers will be escalated until those exact inputs are
+current. No source is dropped and no source-retrieval failure remains open.

