+      url: https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf
+      locator: "Chapter IX §1.A–1.B, printed pp. 404–407: complete metrizable locally convex spaces, compact operators and the Schwartz perturbation theorem."
+    - title: Henri Cartan, Un théorème de finitude
+      url: https://www.numdam.org/item/SHC_1953-1954__6__A17_0.pdf
+      locator: "Exposé 17, pp. 1–3 and 8–10: compact-convergence Fréchet spaces of holomorphic functions and the coherent-section quotient topology."
+verification:
+  precheck: pending
+page: qftx-gaga-compact-coherent-finiteness
+category: quantum-field-theory-mathematics
+---
+
+## Definition
+
+A **Fréchet space** over $\mathbb C$ is a complex vector space $E$ with a Hausdorff locally convex vector-space topology generated by a countable family of continuous seminorms, for which there is a complete metric inducing that topology. A seminorm is a function $p:E\to[0,\infty)$ satisfying $p(x+y)\le p(x)+p(y)$ and $p(cx)=|c|p(x)$ for $x,y\in E$ and $c\in\mathbb C$; locally convex means that every point has a neighborhood basis of convex sets.
+
+## Definition references
+
+[Jean-Pierre Demailly, *Complex Analytic and Differential Geometry*, Chapter IX §1.A–1.B](https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf)
+
+[Henri Cartan, *Un théorème de finitude*, Exposé 17](https://www.numdam.org/item/SHC_1953-1954__6__A17_0.pdf)
